{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":240069,"duration_api_ms":240020,"num_turns":1,"result":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge in observable behavior. This project derives formal specs from C source code, generates Go implementations using an AI coding agent (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: A four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify) with shared infrastructure:\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness (code exists)\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions (partial code: fileinfo only)\n- `pkg/format/` — output formatting: columns, color, human-readable sizes (code exists)\n- `cmd/` — per-utility Go implementations (none on working branch)\n- `magefiles/` — build targets (scaffolded, not a generation target per DD7)\n\n**Implementation State**: The `source_code` field shows production code + tests for `pkg/format` (color, column, size) and `pkg/testutils` (difftest). `pkg/sys` has implementation files (fileinfo.go, fileinfo_darwin.go, fileinfo_linux.go) but **no test file** (testfiles: 0 per code_status). No `cmd/` utilities exist on the working branch.\n\n**Current Release**: Release 00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure) is the earliest incomplete release. Within it:\n- uc002-format: code + tests exist → effectively complete\n- uc004-testutils: code + tests exist → effectively complete\n- uc003-sys: implementation exists but **no tests** → incomplete\n- uc001-magefiles: scaffolded (DD7), only cmd/version is a generation target → not started\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nPer P1 (release-driven priority), release 00.0 is the focus. The `pkg/sys` package has implementation code (Stat, Lstat, FileMetadata covering prd002-sys R2.1–R2.3) but zero tests. Per P8 (implementation before tests), the implementation exists, so tests are the canonical next step. This unblocks confidence in the foundational layer before building `cmd/` utilities that depend on it.\n\nThe task creates `pkg/sys/fileinfo_test.go`, which:\n- Completes the test coverage gap in release 00.0 uc003-sys\n- Follows the existing test patterns (external test package, table-driven subtests, doc comments referencing PRD requirements)\n- Is within line budget (~150–200 lines)\n- Anchors to known PRD sub-requirements visible in the source code comments\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd002-sys R2.1-R2.3: tests for Stat, Lstat, and FileMetadata\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd002-sys.yaml (R2.1-R2.3 requirements for file metadata)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test suite spec for release 00.0)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (implementation under test -- Stat, Lstat, FileMetadata)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo_darwin.go (Darwin-specific newFileMetadata extracting Mtimespec)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo_linux.go (Linux-specific newFileMetadata extracting Mtim)\n      - pkg/format/color_test.go (project test style -- doc comments, table-driven subtests, t.Parallel)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/sys/fileinfo_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for Stat, Lstat, and FileMetadata accessors\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test that Stat returns correct FileMetadata for a regular file and follows symlinks to the target per prd002-sys R2.1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test that Lstat returns metadata for the symlink itself without following it per prd002-sys R2.1\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test that FileMetadata.ModTime returns the file modification time matching the value set on disk per prd002-sys R2.2\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test that FileMetadata.Blocks returns a non-negative 512-byte block count for regular files per prd002-sys R2.2\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Test that Stat and Lstat return a non-nil error wrapping the path for non-existent files per prd002-sys R2.1\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use //go:build darwin || linux build tag matching the source files fileinfo.go, fileinfo_darwin.go, and fileinfo_linux.go\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use external test package (package sys_test) matching the project convention in pkg/format/color_test.go and pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Create temporary files and symlinks via t.TempDir() and os.Symlink for isolated test fixtures\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/sys/fileinfo_test.go exists with //go:build darwin || linux tag and package sys_test\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/sys/ passes with all tests green\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests verify that Stat on a symlink returns metadata of the target file, while Lstat returns metadata of the symlink itself\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Tests verify that ModTime on a newly created file returns a time within the last 60 seconds\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Tests verify that Blocks returns a value greater than or equal to zero for a non-empty regular file\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"Tests verify that Stat and Lstat return a non-nil error when the path does not exist\"\n```","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"ead192ac-8c22-4fb0-ad42-78c4e48c690a","total_cost_usd":0.342473,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":61726,"output_tokens":12464,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12464,"cacheReadInputTokens":61726,"cacheCreationInputTokens